<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνῠ-σις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνύω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>accomplishment,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. δ᾽ οὐκ ἔσσεται αὐτῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.347
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἄνυσίν τινα δήομεν</span>
			we find no <i>end, accomplish</i> nothing, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.544
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρήμασιν ὧν ἄ. γίνεται οὐδεμία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					462
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδ᾽ ἄνυσις</span> there is no
				<i>respite,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.93
			</span></i>.—Poet. and late Prose, as <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.77b
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
